e the movie was a  large growing experience for the young  actress and everybody ended up getting  along just fine  in fact they eventually became one big  happy family we guess we can't really  complain about that one detail too much  since it did make for some on point  Sharpay drama another member of the  wildcat squad he was also a lot like her  on-screen character when she took on the  role of taylor mckessie is none other  than  Monique Coleman Monique was actually  very close to quitting acting all  together before landing a role in High  School Musical the ultimate reason she  did end up auditioning was that she  wanted to represent a smart and sweet  african-american character who her  nieces and God's sisters could relate to  at the time the only other prominent  african-american actress to appear on  the Disney Channel was Raven Symone from  Disney's that So Raven  this made Taylor's decision a majorly  awesome and brave one funny enough both  Ashley and Monique auditioned for the  roles of Gabriella as well but Monique  mentioned that she was not very  interested in landing the specific role  and felt totally out of place singing  and dancing for the part during the  audition process that worked out pretty  well for our girl since we just couldn't  imagine anyone else playing Taylor's  part one thing that the entire cast  always mentioned was just how close they  grew while filming the three movies they  also boasted about how much fun it was  to work together a fun fact for all of  you is that Ashley Tisdale and Monique  Coleman had actually already met on the  set of The Suite Life of Zack and Cody  so the girls were already pretty excited  to be working together again another  pretty funny story behind the High  School Musical audition process is that  they took place in a trailer with some  pretty thin walls so a lot of what was  going on during the audition process  could clearly be heard by everyone else  auditioning Lucas Grabeel who ended up  playing Ryan Evans mentioned that he  also auditioned for the role of Troy  Bolton but was completely shook after  hearing his co-star Drew Seeley seeing  in the audition room despite already  being a prominent Disney star drew  didn't end up landing the role of Troy  Bolton but that didn't mean that he  didn't get to play a pretty major role  in the movie franchise not only did he  get to sing all the tracks in the first  High School Musical movie but he also  replaced Zac Efron on tour when he was  too busy filming for hairspray drew also  wrote the lyrics behind the catchy song  gets ahead in the game and later went on  to star in another cinderella story  featuring the prominent Disney celeb  Selena Gomez Disney was a pretty  tight-knit celebrity community back in  the day which led to a whole lot of  movie crossovers and guest star features  Selena Gomez herself was actually meant  to guess star and one of the movies  particularly High School Musical 2 but  she apparently decided to reject the  offer to pursue more serious acting  Miley Cyrus on the other hand he was  already famous for her role as Hannah  Montana  maybe an iconic appearance at the end of  the second movie during the all-4-one  performance a little fun fact that not a  lot of people know is that there were  actually official online polls where the  fans got to vote for some pretty cool  things like which member of the Hannah  Montana cast would make a great  appearance and which desert Zeki should  give shar-pei in the first movie does  anyone remember what he ended up giving  her try letting us know in the comments  here's a little behind the scenes secret  you probably don't know about there is a  cast member who wore a t-shirt with the  words I love waffles sewn across it in  the first movie can you guys guess who  it is  well if you guessed Corbin Bleu then  you're totally right after noticing the  t-shirt in a wardrobe fitting Corbin  decided that iconic t-shirts would be a  staple in his character Chad's wardrobe  Corbin continued to trends by creating  his very own t-shirts all of which had  funny catchphrases and sayings on them  so what happened to all these unique  t-shirts  well Corbin still holding on to them  sadly they're being stored and not used  but still we're happy to know that  Corbin is holding on to some of his high  school musical memorabilia to end this  video on a sweet note we think it is  definitely worth mentioning that the  director of the franchise Kimmy Ortega  actually had a special yawning jar on  set which he used in a pretty funny way  every time a cast member yond on set  they were made to put money into this  jar this money would later be donated to  a charity of their choosing during the  Christmas season this was a great way  for the entire cast to stay motivated it  also ensured that the cast's on-screen  energy was spot-on  we absolutely loved the High School  Musical movies and we have to admit  Sharpay was our favorite character let  us know who your favorite character was  in the comments section below  and that's a wrap thanks for watching  the things be sure to give this video a  big thumbs up and don't forget to  subscribe for the latest Disney Channel  news we'll catch you next time  [Music]
 

